# Iron Linux - live medium + installer package list
#
# Packages that make the ISO behave as a live/bootable medium and let a
# user install Iron Linux to disk. live-boot/live-config/live-tools are
# effectively no-ops once installed to a real disk (they only activate
# with `boot=live` on the kernel command line), so it's safe to leave
# them in the installed system rather than special-case their removal.
#
# Calamares is the installer (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md for why: mature,
# distribution-independent, Qt-based but not tied to KDE Plasma, and
# already has a Debian settings module we theme for Iron in a later task).

## --- Debian Live boot/session glue ---
live-boot
live-config
live-tools

## --- Installer ---
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
rsync
cryptsetup
keyutils
efibootmgr
os-prober
x11-xserver-utils
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
btrfs-progs
xfsprogs

## --- Installer runtime dependency: NOT pulled in automatically ---
# Calamares' "displaymanager" python job module does `import toml` (see
# /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/calamares/modules/displaymanager/main.py,
# DMgreetd.config_load) to read/write /etc/greetd/config.toml when greetd
# is the configured display manager (displaymanager.conf). Debian does
# not declare this as a package dependency of calamares (it's a Python
# runtime import, invisible to dpkg), so without it explicitly listed
# here the installer crashes with "Bad main script file" / a
# ModuleNotFoundError partway through every install - found by actually
# running the installer to completion in QEMU, not by static inspection.
python3-toml
